Z||000000||Eric||05-02-2000||03:56 PM||||I have an 88GT which has been modified quite a bit except for the suspension.  I've always felt the 88 suspension was too high in front, but I didn't want to do anything drastic like cutting the springs if fear it might hurt the handling.  I know Rayne makes drop spindles but they're like $550 for the pair.  Does anyone know of any other manufactures?  I am aware that the Fiero Store sold some lowering springs for the 88, but I've heard bad things about them and I believe they've been discontinued.  There was another thread about a month ago that mentioned cutting down a set of eibachs for the earlier Fieros to the height of our 88 front springs.  I think it may have been 88 Fiero who mentioned this because he took a ride in an 88 that had this done.  I autocross this car so handling is way more important than looks.  I may even keep the stock setup if I don't feel there are any better options.  Any opinions?||||reg||5
